# Cloudflare Pages serves static assets with max-age=14400 by default, so a
# stylesheet change took up to four hours to reach a returning visitor. HTML
# is already served max-age=0, which means a CSS change shipped new markup to
# browsers still holding the old stylesheet -- the blog index rendered with
# its previous grid rules and looked broken, which is exactly what happened
# on 2026-10-28.
#
# styles.css is a single hand-maintained file with no content hash in its
# name, so it cannot be cached by version. Revalidate it instead: the ETag
# makes the usual case a 304 with no body, which is cheap.
/styles.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
